diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..76c6f9d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# Credit control - developer notes
+
+**Nothing here has been run.** There was no PHP or database in this environment, so none of it has been executed, linted or
+tested. It was written against the existing code by reading it. Run `php -l` on the new files, apply update 44 to a copy of
+the live database, and walk through the acceptance criteria before shipping.
+
+## The main design decision: stop and watch are the existing credit status
+
+webERP already has the mechanism the business is asking for. Every customer has a credit status
+(`debtorsmaster.holdreason` -> `holdreasons.dissallowinvoices`). `1` blocks the customer at order entry, `2` is a "watch" that
+warns (`SelectOrderItems.php` already handled `2`, but `CreditStatus.php` could only create `0` and `1`).
+So "stop" and "watch" are **not** new fields. Credit control moves customers between three configured statuses
+(normal / watch / stop). That keeps every existing screen, the customer-portal check, statements and the aged debtors
+report in agreement, and means the existing live customers keep their current status (BR-39, BR-40).
+
+Everything else is in new tables, so `debtorsmaster`, `debtortrans` and `salesorders` are **not altered**. Several places
+insert into them by position (`Z_CreateCompany.php`, `Z_ChangeCustomerCode.php`, the demo data), so a new column would have
+broken them.
+
+## What was built
+
+**Database** - `sql/updates/44.php` (upgrade) and the same in `install/sql/tables/*.sql` + `install/sql/data/creditcontrol*.sql`
+(new install; the installer runs one statement per file, hence several small files). Tables: `debtorcredit` (next review date,
+interest/fee exemptions, collection note), `creditreviews`, `creditlog` (audit trail), `dunningstages`, `dunningletters`,
+`dunninglettersdetail`, `creditdisputes`, `creditorderholds`, `latecharges`, `writeoffs`. Also: security tokens 21 and 22,
+four new debtor transaction types, scripts, menu items, config settings, three credit statuses, starter letters, and a next
+review date for every existing customer.
+
+**Shared code** - `includes/CreditControlFunctions.php`: status, audit log, order holds, overdue calculation, and the
+ledger posting (charge, waiver, write off, allocation incl. difference on exchange). Used by the pages, order entry, invoicing and the API.
+
+**New pages**
+| Page | For |
+|---|---|
+| `CreditControlCustomer.php` | credit file: review (limit changes with it), stop/watch/normal, disputes, exemptions, collection note, history |
+| `CreditControlReport.php` | due for review, over limit, on watch/stop; filter by rep and currency; totals in home currency |
+| `CreditControlReminders.php` | reminder run: preview, leave customers out, email, list no-email customers, printable letter |
+| `CreditControlCharges.php` | month-end interest and fee: preview, confirm, waive |
+| `CreditControlWriteOffs.php` | request, Finance Director approval, report |
+| `CreditControlOrders.php` | held orders, open orders for stopped/watched customers, release |
+| `CreditControlSetup.php` | Finance settings, GL accounts, letter stages |
+| `CreditControlImport.php` | go-live csv of the spreadsheet (stop list, limits, review dates) |
+| `CustomerCreditAccount.php` | read-only view for customers (portal), reps and office staff |
+
+**Existing code changed, and why**
+- `CreditStatus.php`: three-way effect (OK / watch / stop) instead of a checkbox; cannot delete a status credit control uses.
+- `Customers.php`: only credit control can change limit or status (fields disabled, and ignored server side); new customers
+  get the default limit, normal status and a review date; changes are logged. `Z_ImportDebtors.php`, `api_customers.php`: review date on create.
+- Blocking new orders on a stopped customer on every route: `DeliveryDetails.php` (sales office / portal), `api_salesorders.php`
+  (web shop; new error 1158), `EDIProcessOrders.php`, `RecurringSalesOrdersProcess.php` (also stops auto-invoicing).
+  `SelectOrderItems.php`: a customer on watch could not place their own order - fixed.
+- `ConfirmDispatch_Invoice.php`: it had **no** hold check at all, so existing orders were invoiced for stopped customers. Now blocked unless released.
+- Over-limit hold: new `Check Credit Limits` option 3 (`SystemParameters.php`); orders are held in `DeliveryDetails.php`, API order lines, EDI and recurring orders.
+- `AgedDebtors.php`: credit status, limit, last reminder stage.
+- `CustomerInquiry.php`, `CustomerAccount.php`: watch showed as "ACCOUNT ON HOLD"; now says watch for staff and nothing for customers. Links to the credit pages.
+- Ledger agreement: charges and write offs are new debtor types (51-54) so `CustomerBalancesMovement.php`,
+  `DebtorsAtPeriodEnd.php` and `Z_CheckDebtorsControl.php` had to learn them. `Z_CheckDebtorsControl.php` now also lists which
+  transactions or journals explain a difference (BR-38). `Z_ChangeCustomerCode.php` renames the new tables' rows.
+- `DatabaseTranslations.php`, `doc/Manual/ManualAccountsReceivable.html` (staff guide + note for sales staff), `doc/NEWS.md`.
+
+## Decisions on the open questions
+1. Interest: simple annual rate, one twelfth a month, on the balance more than N grace days past due (end of month), not disputed. One rate for all currencies/countries.
+2. Fee: one flat fee per customer per month, held in home currency and converted to the customer's currency.
+3. No interest on interest or fees (they are excluded from the base). They can still be chased.
+4. No automatic stop after the final letter. Those customers are listed for Maria to decide.
+5. Over-limit orders are **held for approval** on every route (incl. web shop and standing orders), not rejected. Existing systems keep their current Check Credit Limits value; new installs default to the hold option. **Set it to "Hold" at go-live.**
+6. Write-off threshold is a setting (default 500 in home currency). Only the Finance Director approves, not the accountant, and not their own request.
+7. A written-off debt later paid shows as an unallocated receipt; reclassify with a journal. No special handling built.
+8. Reps see the status and its reason.
+9. Letters are in one language (the wording Finance sets). Not per customer language.
+10. Customers never see watch (portal pages, inquiry, account screens). They are told when on stop.
+11. If neither Maria nor the deputy is there: give any other user the credit control token (role setup). Not built into the software.
+12. Each branch/customer account has its own limit; groups are not modelled.
+
+Other choices: reminder progress is judged on the invoices already chased (pay them and the customer starts again at stage 1); a customer whose balance is nil
+after unallocated receipts is not chased or charged; "accounts contact" is the customer contacts flagged to receive statements.
+Disputes, exemptions and stage progress sit in their own tables so history is kept. The audit tables are insert-only in the application (no edit or delete screens); there are no database triggers.
+
+## Go-live
+1. Upgrade (runs update 44). Everyone gets a review date 12 months out; every existing status is kept.
+2. Give tokens 21 (credit controller and deputy) and 22 (Finance Director - who also needs 21) to roles in Security Roles. Only the System Administrator role has them by default. No other role does, so sales and AR clerks cannot change limits or status.
+3. Credit Control Settings: GL accounts for interest, fees and bad debt (nothing posts until set), rate, fee, grace days, limit, letters.
+4. Load the spreadsheet with Load Credit Status from .csv (check-only first). Stop-list customers must be `stop`.
+5. System Parameters: Check Credit Limits = hold.
+
+## Known gaps
+- `api_customers.php` can still change limit/status for an authenticated API user.
+- Charges are not taxed. Charges go on the customer's first branch.
+- A hold applies when an order is saved; the web-shop API holds when lines are added.
+- Locale (`.po`) files not regenerated. A few new messages are English only until they are.
